      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the finalize hook for objects freed by counting (`free_all`). Cycle collection doesn\u0027t call it: `run_epoch` in `epoch.rs` builds its own `finalize` closure for `S::collect_cycles`, which handles `retire` and `retire_module` but not `retire_syntax`.\n\nSo a syntax object reachable only from a garbage cycle keeps its slot and its Rust `Syntax`, still counts toward `max_syntaxes`, and never returns its charge. A cyclic list or a `letrec` closure is enough. Reproduced:\n- One syntax object off a self-referencing pair, dropped, then `collect_garbage()` twice, per round. Every counting strategy hit `LimitExceeded(Syntaxes)` at round 5 with `max_syntaxes \u003d 5`, with nothing live.\n- At Scheme level, 100,000 rounds of `(let ((p (list s))) (set-cdr! p p))` ended with 100,001 \"live\" slots.\n\nFix: give that closure the `retire_syntax` case (or have both call one function, so they can\u0027t drift again), and add a test that frees a syntax object through a cycle.",
      "revId": "807b57e0afaf1b38149d52cf4674818b14087ed7",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
